    { prompt: "Apply it: recreate the “I will be outspent” email pattern for a PMT class that isn't full. Write the email plus three subject lines to A/B test.", fields: ["Subject line A / B / C", "Opening line (first person, honest stakes)", "Proof line (how many people already acted)", "The small, specific ask + deadline", "Sign-off"], rubric: ["Reads like a personal note from one named person, not a newsletter", "Honest stakes (no invented scarcity)", "Social proof with a real number", "One small, specific ask with a real deadline, and at least 3 subject lines to test"], model: "**Subject A:** I have 4 seats left\n**Subject B:** Saturday's class (honest update)\n**Subject C:** Quick question about riding this spring\n\nFriend,\n\nSaturday's beginner class has 4 open seats, and after Friday at noon I can't add anyone.\n\n[Number] people have learned to ride with us this year; most had never sat on a motorcycle.\n\nIf you've been thinking about it, this is the easiest weekend to start: [book here].\n\nZach, for the PMT team\n\n(Send A/B/C to equal thirds of the list; resend the winner to non-openers 24 hours later.)" }
