    { prompt: "Apply it: recreate the NYT metered-model pattern for ZDub: give a set amount of real value free, then a clear wall where the paid service starts.", fields: ["What's free (your “10 articles”)", "Where the meter stops", "What's behind the wall (paid)", "How the free part builds the habit"], rubric: ["The free part is genuinely useful, not a teaser", "The meter is clear and countable", "The paid offer is the natural next step after the free part", "It keeps the relationship going (no all-or-nothing wall)"], model: "**Free:** a monthly “Ad Teardown” email: 3 local ads rewritten with before/after, plus one free 15-minute audit call per business per year.\n**Meter:** one audit per year; teardowns are public examples, not their own ads.\n**Wall:** a full account audit with a written plan ($X), or done-for-you management.\n**Habit:** the monthly email makes Zach the person owners think of when ads stop working." }
